message.content:
**CSS‑only rotating card**

Below is a minimal example that shows how you can create a “card” that flips (rotates around its Y‑axis) when the mouse hovers over it.  
All the magic happens in CSS – no JavaScript required.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣  Basic reset & layout ---------- */
body{
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    min-height:100vh;
    margin:0;
    background:#f0f0f0;
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣  Card container (perspective) ---------- */
.card-wrapper{
    width:260px;          /* width of the card */
    height:360px;         /* height of the card */
    perspective:800px;    /* gives depth to the 3D effect */
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣  Card itself (front + back) ---------- */
.card{
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    position:relative;
    transform-style:preserve-3d;   /* keep children in 3D space */
    transition:transform .6s ease; /* smooth rotation */
}

.card:hover{
    transform:rotateY(180deg);     /* flip on hover */
}

/* ---------- 4️⃣  Front side ---------- */
.card .front,
.card .back{
    position:absolute;
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    backface-visibility:hidden;    /* hide backside while turned */
    border-radius:12px;
    overflow:hidden;
    box-shadow:0 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,.15);
}

.card .front{
    background:#fff;
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

.card .front img{
    max-width:80%;
    border-radius:8px;
    margin-bottom:15px;
}

.card .front h3{
    margin:0;
    font-size:1.5rem;
    color:#333;
}

.card .front p{
    margin-top:10px;
    font-size:.9rem;
    color:#666;
}

/* ---------- 5️⃣  Back side ---------- */
.card .back{
    background:#fafafa;
    transform:rotateY(180deg);      /* start rotated so it's hidden */
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

.card .back h3{
    margin:0;
    font-size:1.4rem;
    color:#444;
}

.card .back p{
    margin-top:10px;
    font-size:.95rem;
    color:#555;
}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <!-- Front -->
        <div class="front">
            <img src="https://picsum.photos/200/150" alt="Sample image">
            <h3>Tytuł karty</h3>
            <p>To jest przykładowy opis frontu karty.</p>
        </div>
        <!-- Back -->
        <div class="back">
            <h3>Backside Title</h3>
            <p>Treść z tyłu karty pojawia się po obróceniu.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens |
|------|--------------|
| **1** | `perspective` on `.card-wrapper` creates a 3‑D environment. |
| **2** | `transform-style: preserve-3d` keeps child elements in 3‑D space. |
| **3** | `backface-visibility: hidden` hides the backside of each face when it’s turned away from the viewer. |
| **4** | On hover, the whole `.card` rotates 180° around the Y‑axis (`rotateY(180deg)`), revealing the back face. |
| **5** | Transition makes the flip smooth (`transition: transform .6s ease`). |

Feel free to adjust dimensions, colors, fonts, or add more content inside the front/back sections. The key properties are `perspective`, `transform-style`, `backface-visibility`, and the `transform: rotateY(...)` on hover. Happy coding!
